WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.125
<v ->So now let's talk about the integration</v>

2
00:00:02.125 --> 00:00:05.349
between the container services of AWS

3
00:00:05.349 --> 00:00:08.040
and your on-premises deployments.

4
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.580
So the first one is Amazon ECS Anywhere

5
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.080
which allows you to easily run containers

6
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.738
on customer-managed infrastructure,

7
00:00:14.738 --> 00:00:18.240
so that means your on-premises servers, your VMs, and so on.

8
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.758
And so that allows you to deploy any Amazon ECS task

9
00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:23.781
in any environment.

10
00:00:23.781 --> 00:00:27.270
So we have the Cloud and our Corporate Data Center

11
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.594
and we're going to leverage the ECS Service,

12
00:00:29.594 --> 00:00:34.370
the ECS Control Plane to manage our containers on-premises.

13
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:37.199
So for this, we need to install the ECS Container Agent

14
00:00:37.199 --> 00:00:41.070
and the SSM Agent on-premises on our servers,

15
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.851
and then we will specify the external launch type

16
00:00:43.851 --> 00:00:46.362
for our services and our tasks.

17
00:00:46.362 --> 00:00:47.580
And so therefore,

18
00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.160
the ECS Agent will register with the ECS Cluster.

19
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.111
The SSM agent will register with the SSM Service,

20
00:00:53.111 --> 00:00:56.400
and then from there, we can use the ECS Service directly

21
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.660
from the console on AWS to launch our containers.

22
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.650
So as you can see,

23
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.257
there is a tight connection and an internet connection

24
00:01:04.257 --> 00:01:08.017
between your Cloud and your On-Premises Data Center

25
00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:11.168
which allows you to use the ECS Service to connect

26
00:01:11.168 --> 00:01:15.240
and launch containers on your corporate data center.

27
00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.944
So you must have a stable connection

28
00:01:16.944 --> 00:01:20.729
to your designated AWS region.

29
00:01:20.729 --> 00:01:23.216
So the use cases for Amazon ECS Anywhere

30
00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:27.146
is to meet compliance, regulatory, and latency requirements

31
00:01:27.146 --> 00:01:30.237
and to run apps outside of AWS Regions

32
00:01:30.237 --> 00:01:32.124
and closer to other services

33
00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:34.200
which allows you to perform, for example,

34
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.880
some on-premises machine learning,

35
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.069
videos processing, data processing, and so on.

36
00:01:39.069 --> 00:01:42.761
So here we bring the benefits of ECS on-premises

37
00:01:42.761 --> 00:01:46.273
and we need an internet connection between the two.

38
00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:48.304
Now for Amazon EKS Anywhere,

39
00:01:48.304 --> 00:01:49.865
even though the name is similar,

40
00:01:49.865 --> 00:01:52.650
the concepts are a little bit different.

41
00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.965
So here, we want to create and operate Kubernetes Cluster

42
00:01:55.965 --> 00:01:57.944
created outside of AWS.

43
00:01:57.944 --> 00:02:00.007
So you're on your On-Premises Data Center,

44
00:02:00.007 --> 00:02:02.868
you're going to create an EKS Cluster.

45
00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:06.417
For this, we will leverage the Amazon EKS Distro,

46
00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:10.075
which is the Amazon's flavor of Kubernetes,

47
00:02:10.075 --> 00:02:13.233
that's their own release with a bit more tools on top of it,

48
00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.484
and that's the one they use to run Amazon EKS Service.

49
00:02:16.484 --> 00:02:18.317
So you can install the same Distro

50
00:02:18.317 --> 00:02:21.568
that they use to run EKS on-premises.

51
00:02:21.568 --> 00:02:24.863
And the reason why you would use the Amazon EKS Distro

52
00:02:24.863 --> 00:02:26.935
is to reduce support costs

53
00:02:26.935 --> 00:02:30.415
and avoid maintaining redundant third-party tools.

54
00:02:30.415 --> 00:02:35.154
So as you can see, this works without any connection to AWS.

55
00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:39.317
So to get this EKS Cluster started on-premises,

56
00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:43.047
you must use the EKS Anywhere installer.

57
00:02:43.047 --> 00:02:46.254
Then, if you somehow, but this is optional,

58
00:02:46.254 --> 00:02:48.846
wanted to connect the EKS Cluster,

59
00:02:48.846 --> 00:02:52.184
the EKS Anywhere Cluster into AWS,

60
00:02:52.184 --> 00:02:54.451
you could use the EKS Connector,

61
00:02:54.451 --> 00:02:56.272
and using the EKS Connector,

62
00:02:56.272 --> 00:03:00.600
now, Amazon EKS can manage your EKS Cluster on-premises,

63
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.042
which gives you different modes.

64
00:03:02.042 --> 00:03:03.480
So you have to define a mode,

65
00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.507
and you can be either in fully connected

66
00:03:05.507 --> 00:03:07.698
or partially disconnected mode.

67
00:03:07.698 --> 00:03:09.759
That means that there is a connection

68
00:03:09.759 --> 00:03:13.025
between your On-Premises Data Center and Amazon EKS,

69
00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.480
and therefore, we can use the EKS Console

70
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.761
to manage our Amazon EKS Cluster on-premises.

71
00:03:19.761 --> 00:03:22.675
The other mode is a fully disconnected mode

72
00:03:22.675 --> 00:03:26.509
in which case, we don't have a connection to AWS,

73
00:03:26.509 --> 00:03:28.540
we just install the EKS Distro

74
00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.341
and then we leverage open-source tools on-premises

75
00:03:31.341 --> 00:03:33.358
to manage your clusters.

76
00:03:33.358 --> 00:03:35.130
So this gives you different modes,

77
00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.855
but nonetheless, with a fully disconnected mode,

78
00:03:36.855 --> 00:03:40.128
we can get the benefits of an EKS cluster on-premises

79
00:03:40.128 --> 00:03:43.980
without having a connection into AWS.

80
00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.289
Okay, so that's it for this lecture.

81
00:03:45.289 --> 00:03:48.933
I hope you liked it, and I will see you in the next lecture.

